00:11:39,450 --> 00:11:41,010
Yeah, killer moves on the dance floor.

262
00:11:41,250 --> 00:11:41,550
Okay.

263
00:11:41,870 --> 00:11:44,790
Another interesting thing is that he said math schmath.

264
00:11:45,350 --> 00:11:47,530
Now schmath isn't really a word.

265
00:11:47,770 --> 00:11:54,590
No, but this is a really common structure we use in English when we want to sort of take away from the importance of an idea.

266
00:11:54,970 --> 00:11:55,410
Okay.

267
00:11:55,430 --> 00:11:56,890
So you're saying it's not important.

268
00:11:57,070 --> 00:12:00,210
I don't care about it or it's not worth it.

269
00:12:00,330 --> 00:12:00,450
Yeah.

270
00:12:00,470 --> 00:12:02,130
So for example, I'm on a diet.

271
00:12:02,730 --> 00:12:02,970
Right.

272
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:04,760
And I would say diet schmath.

273
00:12:04,760 --> 00:12:05,760
Yeah.

274
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:10,240
So basically the structure is just added sh and then just kind of make it rhyme.

275
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:11,240
Yeah.

276
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:13,440
Schmath or like.

277
00:12:13,440 --> 00:12:14,440
Like work schmirk.

278
00:12:14,630 --> 00:12:14,830
Yeah.

279
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:16,570
Work schmirk or something like that.

280
00:12:16,720 --> 00:12:17,720
Yeah.

281
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:19,170
So you're making fun of it and you're taking away importance.

282
00:12:19,570 --> 00:12:19,710
Yeah.

283
00:12:19,790 --> 00:12:21,470
That's a pretty neat phrase.

284
00:12:21,470 --> 00:12:22,270
And one more.

285
00:12:23,330 --> 00:12:25,230
We heard them say duh.

286
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:26,270
Duh.

287
00:12:26,590 --> 00:12:30,430
So when we say this, we're just saying like, you should know this, stupid.

288
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:31,640
Yeah.

289
00:12:31,640 --> 00:12:32,640
This is obvious.

290
00:12:32,640 --> 00:12:33,640
Yeah.

291
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:38,200
It's kind of making fun of the person or just saying it's so obvious, how can you not know it?

292
00:12:39,200 --> 00:12:40,200
Yeah.

293
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:42,680
And it always goes either at the beginning or at the end of a sentence.

294
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:43,680
Yeah.

295
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:45,180
So duh, Marco, we're recording a podcast.

296
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:46,800
Right.

297
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:47,000
Very good.

298
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:53,100
So some great words and phrases in this dialogue and a little bit of slang as well so you can use it maybe with your friends.

299
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:53,600
That's right.

300
